      "date": "June 5, 2026",
      "image": "images/blog-boost-google-reviews.png",
      "author": "Marcus Williams",
      "category": "Product Guide",
      "readTime": "11 min read",
      "content": "<h2>Why Google Reviews Are Now a Core Business Asset</h2>\n<p>A few years ago, Google reviews were a nice-to-have. Today, they are a non-negotiable part of how local businesses compete online. Studies show that 93% of consumers say online reviews influence their purchasing decisions, and businesses with more than 50 reviews generate significantly more clicks and calls than those with fewer.</p>\n<p>This guide explains how verified Phone Verified Accounts (PVA) can be used responsibly to help businesses build their review presence — and how to think about this tool as part of a broader, long-term reputation strategy.</p>\n\n<h2>What Is a Verified PVA Account and Why Does It Matter for Reviews?</h2>\n<p>A Phone Verified Account (PVA) is a Google account created and authenticated using a real, unique phone number. Google's internal scoring system weights reviews from older, established accounts more heavily than reviews from brand-new or unverified profiles.</p>\n<p>Aged, verified PVA accounts provide the trust signals that Google's algorithm looks for — account history, phone verification, and genuine usage patterns — making the reviews they leave more likely to stick and be treated as legitimate by the platform. Learn more about our <a href='/product/google-reviews-strengthen-your-local-business-presence-with-real-customer-feedback/'>Google Reviews packages</a> or our <a href='/product/google-reviews-turn-your-star-rating-into-your-most-powerful-sales-tool/'>Google 5 Star Reviews service</a>.</p>\n\n<h2>Step-by-Step: How PVA Accounts Build Review Profiles</h2>\n<p>Choose aged PVA accounts (6–12+ months old) with real phone verification and genuine activity history. Optimize your Google Business Profile with photos, accurate details, and a keyword-rich description before adding reviews.</p>\n<p>Use a gradual delivery schedule — 3 to 5 reviews in week one, increasing steadily over weeks two through four. This mirrors organic review accumulation patterns and avoids Google's spam filters. Ensure review content variation: different lengths, different emphasis, different sentiment — no duplicate text across reviews.</p>\n<p>For security when managing your own accounts, read our guide on <a href='/blog/pva-security-guide/'>how to safely use PVA accounts after purchase</a>.</p>\n\n<h2>The Local SEO Impact of a Strong Review Profile</h2>\n<p>Reviews directly influence your Google prominence score. Businesses with more reviews, higher average ratings, and more frequent review activity consistently outperform competitors in the local map pack — which captures search intent at the moment of decision.</p>\n<p>Moving from 10 to 50 to 100 reviews with a 4.5+ average can mean higher map pack rankings, more calls and direction requests, higher click-through rates, and greater conversion rates. These outcomes are interconnected — and they all start with the review profile.</p>\n\n<h2>Choosing the Right Review Package</h2>\n<p>Starting from scratch (0–10 reviews): the <a href='/product/google-reviews-strengthen-your-local-business-presence-with-real-customer-feedback/'>Google Reviews package</a> from 5 reviews gives you an initial social proof foundation. Building momentum (10–30 reviews): the <a href='/product/google-reviews-turn-your-star-rating-into-your-most-powerful-sales-tool/'>5 Star Reviews package</a> accelerates toward the 50-review threshold. For Trustpilot, explore our <a href='/product/trustpilot-reputation-management-packages/'>Trustpilot review packages</a>.</p>\n\n<h2>Final Thoughts</h2>\n<p>Your Google Business Profile rating is one of the most valuable pieces of digital real estate your business owns. Verified PVA accounts, used correctly, are a legitimate tool for building that foundation. Browse our <a href='/shop/'>full product catalog</a> to explore the review packages that match your business goals, or <a href='/contact/'>contact our support team</a> for a custom review strategy.</p>"
